[6.271726, "o", "cat /app/docs/report-schema.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[6.272644, "o", "# Loam audit report contract\r\n\r\nThis document is the normative grading reference for `/app/bin/loam audit`\r\nJSON output and for fresh ingest artifacts. Architecture and rollout notes are\r\nbackground only; when they disagree with this file, this file wins.\r\n\r\n## Audit JSON\r\n\r\nUTF-8 JSON object written to the report path passed to `audit`.\r\n\r\n| Key | Type | Meaning |\r\n| --- | --- | --- |\r\n| `status` | string | Always the literal `complete` when the run finishes successfully. |\r\n| `cases` | array | One object per `.case` file, in bytewise filename order. |\r\n| `digest` | string | Non-empty hex digest of the serialized `cases` body. |\r\n\r\n### Each element of `cases`\r\n\r\n| Key | Type | Meaning |\r\n| --- | --- | --- |\r\n| `case_id` | string | Identifier from the case line. |\r\n| `row_count` | integer | Number of qualifying live rows included in the answer. |\r\n| `sum_amount` | integer | Sum of amounts for those qualifying live rows. |\r\n| `pages_total` | integer | Number of slabs present in the store for the case. |\r\n| `pa"]
[6.272696, "o", "ges_read` | integer | Number of slabs actually opened for the case. |\r\n| `path` | string | Execution lane used: `row` or `batch`. |\r\n| `skipping` | boolean | Whether selective admission was requested for the case. |\r\n\r\n`row_count`, `sum_amount`, `pages_total`, and `pages_read` are the per-case\r\nanswer and work counters. Equivalent modes on the same store and probe must\r\nagree on `row_count` and `sum_amount`. Selective healthy controls must keep\r\n`pages_read` strictly below `pages_total` while still returning the correct\r\nanswer. Repeated identical audits must emit byte-identical report files.\r\n\r\n## Fresh ingest artifact\r\n\r\n`/app/bin/loam ingest <CSV> <store-directory>` writes exactly:\r\n\r\n`<store-directory>/data.store`\r\n\r\nNo other store filename is accepted for grading.\r\n\r\n## Faithful live-value markers\r\n\r\nEach slab in a store carries numeric markers `low`, `high`, and `has_absent`.\r\n\r\n- `low` and `high` span only live amounts in that slab.\r\n- `has_absent` is true when the slab contains any non-live entry.\r\n- "]
[6.27273, "o", "A slab whose entries are all non-live records `low` 0, `high` 0, and\r\n  `has_absent` true.\r\n- Fresh ingest must keep those markers faithful to the live-value domain of the\r\n  CSV it wrote. Archived mixed-generation stores keep their on-disk markers;\r\n  readers must interpret them without rewriting the artifact.\r\n"]
[6.272848, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[6.6035, "i", "/app/bin/loam audit /app/data/cases /app/output/audit.json && cat /app/output/audit.json\n"]
[6.603797, "o", "/app/bin/loam audit /app/data/cases /app/output/audit.json && cat /app/output/audit.json\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[6.60786, "o", "{\"status\":\"complete\",\"cases\":[{\"case_id\":\"c_legit\",\"row_count\":1,\"sum_amount\":-999,\"pages_total\":2,\"pages_read\":1,\"path\":\"batch\",\"skipping\":true},{\"case_id\":\"h_skip\",\"row_count\":4,\"sum_amount\":460,\"pages_total\":3,\"pages_read\":1,\"path\":\"batch\",\"skipping\":true},{\"case_id\":\"h_full\",\"row_count\":4,\"sum_amount\":460,\"pages_total\":3,\"pages_read\":3,\"path\":\"row\",\"skipping\":false},{\"case_id\":\"h_region\",\"row_count\":3,\"sum_amount\":430,\"pages_total\":3,\"pages_read\":3,\"path\":\"row\",\"skipping\":true},{\"case_id\":\"m_range\",\"row_count\":2,\"sum_amount\":70,\"pages_total\":4,\"pages_read\":1,\"path\":\"row\",\"skipping\":true},{\"case_id\":\"m_narrow\",\"row_count\":0,\"sum_amount\":0,\"pages_total\":4,\"pages_read\":0,\"path\":\"row\",\"skipping\":true},{\"case_id\":\"m_null\",\"row_count\":1,\"sum_amount\":0,\"pages_total\":4,\"pages_read\":4,\"path\":\"batch\",\"skipping\":false},{\"case_id\":\"m_interact\",\"row_count\":1,\"sum_amount\":-5,\"pages_total\":4,\"pages_read\":1,\"path\":\"batch\",\"skipping\":true},{\"case_id\":\"m_neg\",\"row_count\":1,\"sum_amount\":-5,\"pages_total\":4,\"pages_read\":4,\"pa"]
[6.607939, "o", "th\":\"batch\",\"skipping\":false},{\"case_id\":\"m_all\",\"row_count\":11,\"sum_amount\":1096,\"pages_total\":4,\"pages_read\":4,\"path\":\"batch\",\"skipping\":false},{\"case_id\":\"v_window\",\"row_count\":4,\"sum_amount\":132,\"pages_total\":3,\"pages_read\":3,\"path\":\"row\",\"skipping\":true},{\"case_id\":\"v_missing\",\"row_count\":1,\"sum_amount\":0,\"pages_total\":3,\"pages_read\":1,\"path\":\"batch\",\"skipping\":true},{\"case_id\":\"v_check\",\"row_count\":1,\"sum_amount\":0,\"pages_total\":3,\"pages_read\":1,\"path\":\"row\",\"skipping\":true},{\"case_id\":\"v_full\",\"row_count\":2,\"sum_amount\":0,\"pages_total\":3,\"pages_read\":3,\"path\":\"row\",\"skipping\":false}],\"digest\":\"386f5d5d6e94d3e9\"}\r\n"]
[6.608072, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[6.608124, "o", "root@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[12.973443, "i", "cat /app/docs/architecture.md\nprintf '\\n--- format ---\\n'\ncat /app/docs/format-notes.md\nprintf '\\n--- cases ---\\n'\nfor f in /app/data/cases/*.case; do echo \"### $f\"; cat \"$f\"; done\n"]
[12.973576, "o", "cat /app/docs/architecture.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.974524, "o", "# Loam architecture\r\n\r\nLoam is a small offline columnar lab used by release engineering before storage\r\nchanges reach the billing warehouse. `rust/` owns import and compaction. It emits\r\nself-describing slabs with value lanes, presence lanes, origin lanes, text codes,\r\nand compact markers. `cpp/` owns reads. The harbor stage decides which slabs are\r\nneeded, then either the row reader or lattice reader computes a tally. The row\r\nreader walks record structs; the lattice reader consumes per-slab column lanes.\r\n\r\nThe command front end reads every `.case` file in bytewise filename order and\r\nevery record in source order. Structured counters come from the selected reader,\r\nnot from estimates. Artifact files are append-free after creation; a reader must\r\nnot repair them in place.\r\n\r\n`/app/tools/reset-lab` restores the bundled drill data before a clean replay.\r\n\r\nOlder slabs are supported because disaster-recovery snapshots outlive the writer\r\nthat created them. Newer writers can add header generations, but readers r"]
[12.974559, "o", "emain\r\nresponsible for interpreting each slab according to its own header and local\r\nmarkers.\r\n"]
[12.974692, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[12.974716, "o", "root@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[12.974785, "o", "printf '\\n--- format ---\\n'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.97514, "o", "\r\n--- format ---\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# cat /app/docs/format-notes.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.975774, "o", "# Format notes from the v2 rollout\r\n\r\nThese notes were copied from the rollout ticket and may lag the current reader.\r\nThey are useful background only. The operational grading contract for audit JSON,\r\nper-case counters, ingest output naming, and live-value markers is\r\n`/app/docs/report-schema.md`.\r\n\r\nA file begins with `H|generation`. Each `P` record describes one slab, followed\r\nby the declared number of `R` records. The row record carries presence, origin,\r\namount, and region. Marker fields let readers avoid opening slabs for predicates\r\nthat cannot match.\r\n\r\nThe v2 rollout assumed the amount lane remained sufficient to recognize missing\r\nhistorical values because old producers reserved one amount. The later writer\r\nkept origin and presence lanes to support mixed compaction and legitimate values\r\nthat overlap old conventions. If these assumptions conflict, the artifact and a\r\nfull reader are stronger evidence than this note.\r\n"]
[12.975921, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[12.975948, "o", "root@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[12.97601, "o", "printf '\\n--- cases ---\\n'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.97603, "o", "\r\n--- cases ---\r\n"]
[12.976059, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[12.976245, "o", "for f in /app/data/cases/*.case; do echo \"### $f\"; cat \"$f\"; done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.976299, "o", "### /app/data/cases/control.case\r\n"]
[12.977018, "o", "# id|store|operation|x|y|path|skipping|operator note\r\nc_legit|/app/data/archive/current.store|eq|-999|0|batch|1|legitimate overlap\r\nh_skip|/app/data/archive/healthy.store|range|100|130|batch|1|selective control\r\nh_full|/app/data/archive/healthy.store|range|100|130|row|0|full control\r\nh_region|/app/data/archive/healthy.store|region_eq|north|0|row|1|text control\r\n"]
[12.97713, "o", "### /app/data/cases/incident.case\r\n"]
[12.977823, "o", "# id|store|operation|x|y|path|skipping|operator note\r\nm_range|/app/data/archive/mixed.store|range|10|40|row|1|invoice window\r\nm_narrow|/app/data/archive/mixed.store|range|10|20|row|1|narrow window\r\nm_null|/app/data/archive/mixed.store|isnull|0|0|batch|0|missing count\r\nm_interact|/app/data/archive/mixed.store|range|-1000|25|batch|1|mixed window\r\nm_neg|/app/data/archive/mixed.store|range|-100|-1|batch|0|negative window\r\nm_all|/app/data/archive/mixed.store|all|0|0|batch|0|full tally\r\nv_window|/app/data/archive/vault.store|range|10|50|row|1|vault window\r\nv_missing|/app/data/archive/vault.store|isnull|0|0|batch|1|vault absent probe\r\nv_check|/app/data/archive/vault.store|isnull|0|0|row|1|vault absent recheck\r\nv_full|/app/data/archive/vault.store|isnull|0|0|row|0|vault full control\r\n"]
[12.977982, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[12.978009, "o", "root@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[13.314575, "i", "sed -n '1,240p' /app/cpp/src/store.cpp\nprintf '\\n--- row.cpp ---\\n'\nsed -n '1,240p' /app/cpp/src/row.cpp\nprintf '\\n--- parse.cpp ---\\n'\nsed -n '1,220p' /app/cpp/src/parse.cpp\nprintf '\\n--- report.cpp ---\\n'\nsed -n '1,260p' /app/cpp/src/report.cpp\nprintf '\\n--- main.cpp ---\\n'\nsed -n '1,220p' /app/cpp/src/main.cpp\n"]
[13.314726, "o", "sed -n '1,240p' /app/cpp/src/store.cpp\r\n"]
[13.314754, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.31594, "o", "#include \"loam/store.hpp\"\r\n\r\n#include \"loam/exec.hpp\"\r\n"]
[13.315949, "o", "#include \"loam/plan.hpp\"\r\n"]
[13.316004, "o", "\r\n#include <fstream>\r\n#include <stdexcept>\r\n#include <string>\r\n\r\nnamespace loam {\r\nnamespace {\r\n\r\nstd::vector<std::string> split(const std::string& line) {\r\n    std::vector<std::string> fields;\r\n    std::size_t start = 0;\r\n"]
[13.316035, "o", "    while (true) {\r\n        const auto end = line.find('|', start);\r\n        fields.push_back(line.substr(start, end - start));\r\n        if (end == std::string::npos) {\r\n            break;\r\n        }\r\n        start = end + 1;\r\n    }\r\n    return fields;\r\n}\r\n\r\n}  // namespace\r\n\r\n"]
[13.316059, "o", "std::vector<Slab> load_store(const std::filesystem::path& path) {\r\n    std::ifstream input(path);\r\n    if (!input) {\r\n        throw std::runtime_error(\"cannot open store: \" + path.string());\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    std::vector<Slab> slabs;\r\n    std::string line;\r\n    while (std::getline(input, line)) {\r\n        if (line.empty() || line.rfind(\"H|\", 0) == 0) {\r\n            continue;\r\n        }\r\n        const auto page = split(line);\r\n        if (page.size() != 9 || page[0] != \"P\") {\r\n            throw std::runtime_error(\"bad page record in \" + path.string());\r\n        }\r\n        Slab slab;\r\n        slab.id = std::stoull(page[1]);\r\n        slab.generation = static_cast<std::uint8_t>(std::stoul(page[2]));\r\n        slab.low = std::stoll(page[3]);\r\n"]
[13.316078, "o", "        slab.high = std::stoll(page[4]);\r\n        slab.has_absent = page[5] == \"1\";\r\n        slab.region_low = page[6];\r\n        slab.region_high = page[7];\r\n        const auto row_count = std::stoull(page[8]);\r\n        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < row_count; ++i) {\r\n            if (!std::getline(input, line)) {\r\n"]
[13.316096, "o", "                throw std::runtime_error(\"short page in \" + path.string());\r\n            }\r\n            const auto row = split(line);\r\n            if (row.size() != 5 || row[0] != \"R\") {\r\n"]
[13.316118, "o", "                throw std::runtime_error(\"bad row record in \" + path.string());\r\n            }\r\n            const auto presence = static_cast<std::uint8_t>(std::stoul(row[1]));\r\n            const auto origin = static_cast<std::uint8_t>(std::stoul(row[2]));\r\n            const auto amount = std::stoll(row[3]);\r\n            slab.cells.push_back({presence, static_cast<Origin>(origin), amount, row[4]});\r\n            slab.presence_lane.push_back(presence);\r\n            slab.origin_lane.push_back(origin);\r\n            slab.amount_lane.push_back(amount);\r\n            slab.region_lane.push_back(row[4]);\r\n        }\r\n        slabs.push_back(std::move(slab));\r\n    }\r\n    return slabs;\r\n}\r\n"]
[13.316137, "o", "\r\nCaseResult run_case(const CaseSpec& spec) {\r\n    const auto slabs = load_store(spec.store_path);\r\n    Tally total;\r\n    for (const auto& slab : slabs) {\r\n        const Gate gate = turn_b(slab, spec.probe);\r\n        const auto label = turn_d(gate, spec.probe);\r\n        (void)label;\r\n"]
[13.316159, "o", "        const Tally part = spec.probe.lane == Lane::Batch\r\n            ? sweep_c(slab, spec.probe, gate)\r\n            : walk_row(slab, spec.probe, gate);\r\n        total = sweep_e(total, part);\r\n    }\r\n    return {\r\n        spec.case_id,\r\n        total,\r\n        static_cast<std::int64_t>(slabs.size()),\r\n        spec.probe.lane,\r\n        spec.probe.skipping,\r\n    };\r\n"]
[13.316175, "o", "}\r\n\r\n}  // namespace loam\r\n"]
[13.316376, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[13.316391, "o", "root@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[13.31647, "o", "printf '\\n--- row.cpp ---\\n'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.316489, "o", "\r\n--- row.cpp ---\r\n"]
[13.316522, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[13.316635, "o", "sed -n '1,240p' /app/cpp/src/row.cpp\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.317718, "o", "#include \"loam/exec.hpp\"\r\n\r\nnamespace loam {\r\nnamespace {\r\n\r\nbool is_live(const Cell& cell) {\r\n    if (cell.origin == Origin::Retired) {\r\n        return false;\r\n"]
[13.31775, "o", "    }\r\n    if (cell.origin == Origin::Inherited) {\r\n        return true;\r\n    }\r\n    return cell.present != 0;\r\n}\r\n\r\n"]
[13.317776, "o", "bool matches(const Cell& cell, const Probe& probe) {\r\n    switch (probe.op) {\r\n        case Op::All:\r\n            return true;\r\n        case Op::Equal:\r\n            return cell.amount == probe.x;\r\n        case Op::Range:\r\n            return cell.amount >= probe.x && cell.amount <= probe.y;\r\n        case Op::IsNull:\r\n            return false;\r\n        case Op::RegionEqual:\r\n"]
[13.317801, "o", "            return cell.region == probe.text;\r\n    }\r\n    return false;\r\n}\r\n\r\n}  // namespace\r\n\r\nTally walk_row(const Slab& a, const Probe& b, const Gate& c) {\r\n    Tally tally;\r\n    if (!c.read) {\r\n        return tally;\r\n    }\r\n    tally.pages_read = 1;\r\n"]
[13.317828, "o", "    for (const auto& cell : a.cells) {\r\n        const bool live = is_live(cell);\r\n        if (b.op == Op::IsNull) {\r\n            if (!live) {\r\n                ++tally.row_count;\r\n            }\r\n            continue;\r\n        }\r\n        if (live && matches(cell, b)) {\r\n            ++tally.row_count;\r\n            tally.sum_amount += cell.amount;\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n    return tally;\r\n}\r\n"]
[13.317851, "o", "\r\n}  // namespace loam\r\n"]
[13.31802, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[13.318041, "o", "root@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[13.31812, "o", "printf '\\n--- parse.cpp ---\\n'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.318149, "o", "\r\n--- parse.cpp ---\r\n"]
[13.31817, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[13.318279, "o", "sed -n '1,220p' /app/cpp/src/parse.cpp\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.319221, "o", "#include \"loam/store.hpp\"\r\n\r\n#include <algorithm>\r\n#include <fstream>\r\n#include <stdexcept>\r\n#include <string>\r\n\r\nnamespace loam {\r\nnamespace {\r\n\r\n"]
[13.31926, "o", "std::vector<std::string> split(const std::string& line) {\r\n    std::vector<std::string> fields;\r\n    std::size_t start = 0;\r\n    while (true) {\r\n        const auto end = line.find('|', start);\r\n        fields.push_back(line.substr(start, end - start));\r\n        if (end == std::string::npos) {\r\n            break;\r\n        }\r\n        start = end + 1;\r\n    }\r\n    return fields;\r\n}\r\n\r\nOp parse_op(const std::string& value) {\r\n    if (value == \"all\") return Op::All;\r\n    if (value == \"eq\") return Op::Equal;\r\n    if (value == \"range\") return Op::Range;\r\n"]
[13.319283, "o", "    if (value == \"isnull\") return Op::IsNull;\r\n    if (value == \"region_eq\") return Op::RegionEqual;\r\n    throw std::runtime_error(\"unknown operation: \" + value);\r\n}\r\n\r\nLane parse_lane(const std::string& value) {\r\n    if (value == \"row\") return Lane::Row;\r\n    if (value == \"batch\") return Lane::Batch;\r\n    throw std::runtime_error(\"unknown path: \" + value);\r\n}\r\n"]
[13.319304, "o", "\r\n}  // namespace\r\n\r\nstd::vector<CaseSpec> load_cases(const std::filesystem::path& directory) {\r\n    std::vector<std::filesystem::path> paths;\r\n    for (const auto& entry : std::filesystem::directory_iterator(directory)) {\r\n        if (entry.is_regular_file() && entry.path().extension() == \".case\") {\r\n            paths.push_back(entry.path());\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n"]
[13.319324, "o", "    std::sort(paths.begin(), paths.end());\r\n\r\n    std::vector<CaseSpec> cases;\r\n    for (const auto& path : paths) {\r\n        std::ifstream input(path);\r\n        if (!input) {\r\n            throw std::runtime_error(\"cannot open case file: \" + path.string());\r\n        }\r\n        std::string line;\r\n"]
[13.319353, "o", "        while (std::getline(input, line)) {\r\n            if (line.empty() || line[0] == '#') {\r\n                continue;\r\n            }\r\n            const auto fields = split(line);\r\n            if (fields.size() != 8) {\r\n                throw std::runtime_error(\"bad case row in \" + path.string());\r\n            }\r\n            Probe probe;\r\n            probe.op = parse_op(fields[2]);\r\n            if (probe.op == Op::RegionEqual) {\r\n                probe.text = fields[3];\r\n            } else {"]
[13.319378, "o", "\r\n                probe.x = std::stoll(fields[3]);\r\n                probe.y = std::stoll(fields[4]);\r\n            }\r\n            probe.lane = parse_lane(fields[5]);\r\n            probe.skipping = fields[6] == \"1\";\r\n            cases.push_back({fields[0], fields[1], std::move(probe)});\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n    return cases;\r\n"]
[13.3194, "o", "}\r\n\r\n}  // namespace loam\r\n"]
[13.319612, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[13.319637, "o", "root@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[13.319718, "o", "printf '\\n--- report.cpp ---\\n'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.319744, "o", "\r\n--- report.cpp ---\r\n"]
[13.319773, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[13.31979, "o", "root@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[13.319877, "o", "sed -n '1,260p' /app/cpp/src/report.cpp\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.320922, "o", "#include \"loam/report.hpp\"\r\n\r\n#include <fstream>\r\n#include <sstream>\r\n#include <stdexcept>\r\n\r\nnamespace loam {\r\n"]
[13.320961, "o", "namespace {\r\n\r\nstd::string escape_json(const std::string& value) {\r\n    std::string out;\r\n    for (const char ch : value) {\r\n        if (ch == '\"' || ch == '\\\\') {\r\n"]
[13.320994, "o", "            out.push_back('\\\\');\r\n        }\r\n        out.push_back(ch);\r\n    }\r\n    return out;\r\n}\r\n\r\nstd::string cases_json(const std::vector<CaseResult>& cases) {\r\n    std::ostringstream out;\r\n    out << '[';\r\n    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < cases.size(); ++i) {\r\n        if (i != 0) out << ',';\r\n        const auto& item = cases[i];\r\n        out << \"{\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"\" << escape_json(item.case_id)\r\n            << \"\\\",\\\"row_count\\\":\" << item.tally.row_count\r\n            << \",\\\"sum_amount\\\":\" << item.tally.sum_amount\r\n            << \",\\\"pages_total\\\":\" << item.pages_total\r\n            << \",\\\"pages_read\\\":\" << item.tally.pages_read\r\n            << \",\\\"path\\\":\\\"\" << lane_name(item.lane)\r\n            << \"\\\",\\\"skipping\\\":\" << (item.skipping ? \"true\" : \"false\")\r\n            << '}';\r\n    }\r\n"]
[13.321016, "o", "    out << ']';\r\n    return out.str();\r\n}\r\n\r\n}  // namespace\r\n\r\nstd::string lane_name(const Lane lane) {\r\n    return lane == Lane::Batch ? \"batch\" : \"row\";\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid write_report(const std::filesystem::path& path, const std::vector<CaseResult>& cases) {\r\n    if (path.has_parent_path()) {"]
[13.321035, "o", "\r\n        std::filesystem::create_directories(path.parent_path());\r\n    }\r\n    const std::string body = cases_json(cases);\r\n    const std::string digest = digest_hex(body);\r\n    std::ofstream output(path, std::ios::binary | std::ios::trunc);\r\n    if (!output) {\r\n        throw std::runtime_error(\"cannot write report: \" + path.string());\r\n    }\r\n    output << \"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"complete\\\",\\\"cases\\\":\" << body\r\n           << \",\\\"digest\\\":\\\"\" << digest << \"\\\"}\\n\";\r\n}\r\n"]
[13.321046, "o", "\r\n}  // namespace loam\r\n"]
[13.321282, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[13.321328, "o", "root@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[13.321389, "o", "printf '\\n--- main.cpp ---\\n'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.321419, "o", "\r\n--- main.cpp ---\r\n"]
[13.321437, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[13.321552, "o", "sed -n '1,220p' /app/cpp/src/main.cpp\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.322636, "o", "#include \"loam/report.hpp\"\r\n#include \"loam/store.hpp\"\r\n\r\n#include <filesystem>\r\n#include <iostream>\r\n#include <stdexcept>\r\n#include <sys/wait.h>\r\n#include <unistd.h>\r\n#include <vector>\r\n\r\nnamespace {\r\n\r\nint run_ingest(const char* input, const char* output) {\r\n    const pid_t child = fork();\r\n    if (child == -1) {\r\n"]
[13.322685, "o", "        throw std::runtime_error(\"fork failed\");\r\n    }\r\n    if (child == 0) {\r\n        execl(\"/app/bin/loam-ingest\", \"loam-ingest\", input, output, nullptr);\r\n        _exit(127);\r\n    }\r\n    int status = 0;\r\n    if (waitpid(child, &status, 0) == -1) {\r\n        throw std::runtime_error(\"waitpid failed\");\r\n    }\r\n    return WIFEXITED(status) ? WEXITSTATUS(status) : 1;\r\n}\r\n"]
[13.322711, "o", "\r\n}  // namespace\r\n\r\nint main(int argc, char** argv) {\r\n    try {\r\n        if (argc == 4 && std::string(argv[1]) == \"audit\") {\r\n            const auto specs = loam::load_cases(argv[2]);\r\n            std::vector<loam::CaseResult> results;\r\n            results.reserve(specs.size());\r\n            for (const auto& spec : specs) {\r\n                results.push_back(loam::run_case(spec));\r\n            }\r\n            loam::write_report(argv[3], results);\r\n            return 0;\r\n        }\r\n        if (argc == 4 && std::string(argv[1]) == \"ingest\") {\r\n            return run_ingest(argv[2], argv[3]);\r\n        }\r\n        if (argc == 3 && std::string(argv[1]) == \"inspect\") {\r\n            const auto slabs = loam::load_store(argv[2]);\r\n            for (const auto& slab : slabs) {\r\n                std::cout << slab.id << '|' << static_cast<int>(slab.generation)\r\n"]
[13.322746, "o", "                          << '|' << slab.low << '|' << slab.high << '|'\r\n                          << (slab.has_absent ? 1 : 0) << '|' << slab.cells.size()\r\n                          << '\\n';\r\n            }\r\n            return 0;\r\n        }\r\n        std::cerr << \"usage: loam audit <case-directory> <report-path>\\n\"\r\n"]
[13.322768, "o", "                  << \"       loam ingest <csv> <store-directory>\\n\"\r\n                  << \"       loam inspect <store>\\n\";\r\n        return 2;\r\n    } catch (const std::exception& error) {\r\n        std::cerr << \"loam: \" << error.what() << '\\n';\r\n        return 1;\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n"]
[13.322937, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
[13.656267, "i", "sed -n '1,260p' /app/rust/src/main.rs\nprintf '\\n--- codec ---\\n'\nsed -n '1,260p' /app/rust/src/codec.rs\nprintf '\\n--- model ---\\n'\nsed -n '1,220p' /app/rust/src/model.rs\nprintf '\\n--- report ---\\n'\nsed -n '1,220p' /app/rust/src/report.rs\n"]
[13.657396, "o", "sed -n '1,260p' /app/rust/src/main.rs\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.659016, "o", "mod codec;\r\nmod ember;\r\nmod model;\r\nmod report;\r\n\r\nuse ember::pale::{tilt_d, Dial};\r\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\r\n\r\nfn main() {\r\n    if let Err(error) = run() {\r\n"]
[13.659153, "o", "        eprintln!(\"loam-ingest: {error}\");\r\n        std::process::exit(1);\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\nfn run() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {\r\n    let args: Vec<String> = std::env::args().collect();\r\n    if args.len() != 3 {\r\n        return Err(\"usage: loam-ingest <csv> <store>\".into());\r\n    }\r\n    let cells = codec::read_csv(Path::new(&args[1]))?;\r\n    let pages = ember::reed::gather(cells, 4)?;\r\n    let directory = PathBuf::from(&args[2]);\r\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(&directory)?;\r\n    let target = directory.join(\"data.store\");\r\n    codec::write_pages(&target, &pages)?;\r\n\r\n    let size = std::fs::metadata(&target)?.len() as usize;\r\n    let mut dial = Dial::default();\r\n    let cell_count = pages.iter().map(|page| page.cells.len()).sum();\r\n    tilt_d(&mut dial, cell_count, size);\r\n    eprintln!(\"{}\", report::line(&dial));\r\n    Ok(())\r\n}\r\n"]
[13.659466, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[13.659601, "o", "root@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# printf '\\n--- codec ---\\n'"]
[13.659773, "o", "\r\n"]
[13.659911, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.659962, "o", "\r\n"]
[13.660082, "o", "--- codec ---\r\n\u001b[?2004h"]
[13.660308, "o", "root@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# sed -n '1,260p' /app/rust/src/codec.rs"]
[13.660438, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.661729, "o", "use crate::model::{Cell, Page};\r\nuse std::fs::File;\r\nuse std::io::{BufRead, BufReader, BufWriter, Write};\r\n"]
[13.661758, "o", "use std::path::Path;\r\n\r\npub(crate) fn read_csv(path: &Path) -> Result<Vec<Cell>, Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {\r\n    let file = File::open(path)?;"]
[13.661855, "o", "\r\n    let mut rows = Vec::new();"]
[13.66187, "o", "\r\n    for (line_no, line) in BufReader::new(file).lines().enumerate() {\r\n        let line = line?;\r\n        if line_no == 0 && line.starts_with(\"origin,\") {\r\n            continue;\r\n        }\r\n        if line.trim().is_empty() {\r\n            continue;\r\n        }\r\n        let fields: Vec<&str> = line.split(',').collect();\r\n        if fields.len() != 4 {\r\n            return Err(format!(\"{}:{}: expected four columns\", path.display(), line_no + 1).into());\r\n        }"]
[13.661878, "o", "\r\n        rows.push(Cell {"]
[13.661897, "o", "\r\n            origin: fields[0].parse()?,"]
[13.661908, "o", "\r\n            present: fields[1].parse()?,\r\n"]
[13.661918, "o", "            amount: fields[2].parse()?,"]
[13.661926, "o", "\r\n            region: fields[3].trim().to_owned(),\r\n"]
[13.661933, "o", "        });"]
[13.661941, "o", "\r\n    }"]
[13.662001, "o", "\r\n"]
[13.662036, "o", "    Ok(rows)\r\n}\r\n\r\npub(crate) fn write_pages(path: &Path, pages: &[Page]) -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {\r\n    if let Some(parent) = path.parent() {\r\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(parent)?;\r\n    }\r\n    let file = File::create(path)?;\r\n    let mut out = BufWriter::new(file);\r\n    writeln!(out, \"H|3\")?;\r\n    for page in pages {\r\n"]
[13.662165, "o", "        writeln!(\r\n            out,\r\n            \"P|{}|{}|{}|{}|{}|{}|{}|{}\",\r\n            page.id,\r\n            page.generation,\r\n            page.mark.low,\r\n            page.mark.high,\r\n            u8::from(page.mark.has_absent),\r\n            page.region_low,\r\n            page.region_high,\r\n            page.cells.len()\r\n        )?;\r\n        for cell in &page.cells {\r\n            writeln!(\r\n                out,\r\n"]
[13.662206, "o", "                \"R|{}|{}|{}|{}\",\r\n                cell.present, cell.origin, cell.amount, cell.region\r\n"]
[13.662235, "o", "            )?;\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n    out.flush()?;\r\n    Ok(())\r\n"]
[13.66227, "o", "}\r\n"]
[13.662425, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[13.662524, "o", "root@e4e73d3a-e155-4fa8-8263-b589414b053f:/app# "]
